  "answer": "The public covariant branch is stationary but not ghost even already at order lambda. Its nonzero rank-four correction has Laurent support Z^-1, while ghost parity sends it to the independent Z branch. Since the whole pushforward is neutral and Q=0, the Eq. (19) charge formula still holds trivially but its required ghost-even neutral term does not. The canonical odd remainder has relative norm -7/288, not zero, so the published weak-ghost-symmetry mechanism fails on this branch. Adding the kappa-conjugate orbit branch is the unique minimal support repair: its symmetric generator exponentiates to an exact neutral, stationary, ghost-even finite projector. The added branch is not supplied by the public Rt map, so this is an architecture, not a proof of Bateman--Turok's unpublished completion.",
